<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saxony-Anhalt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saxony-Anhalt is a state of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> as its capital. It was formed in 1947 from the Prussian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/province-of-saxony">Province of Saxony</a> and the Free State of Anhalt, dissolved in 1952 and re-established in 1990. Its towns, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>, Halle, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quedlinburg">Quedlinburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a>, hold many medieval and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> sites.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt.jpg" alt="Saxony-Anhalt" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saxony-Anhalt_(state).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
